<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Exports prompt basis hikes.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Exports prompt basis hikes.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>An active soymeal export shipment program by Archer Daniels Midland Co prompted the company to raise soymeal prices to domestic customers to ensure supplies for export customers, soymeal sources said.</p>
<p>ADM officials were unavailable for comment.</p>
<p>Soymeal traders said ADM raised offers for 48 percent soymeal from its Decatur, Ill. plant $6 since Friday to $18 per ton over CBOT March futures. Other dealers said the basis hike is temporary and once exports slow the basis should drop.</p>
<p>Domestic soymeal offers from other processors were mostly unchanged from Friday.  </p>
